---
import CodeBlock from './CodeBlock.astro';
---
<section class="kop-block" id="how">
  <div class="kop-wrap">
    <div class="kop-sechead">
      <span class="kop-eyebrow">How it works</span>
      <h2>Authentication moves to the proxy. Authorization never moves.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="kop-how">
      <div>
        <ol class="kop-olist">
          <li><div><b>Point kubectl at the proxy</b><span>Clients get a kubeconfig whose server is the proxy. The API server's own endpoint keeps working for everyone else.</span></div></li>
          <li><div><b>The proxy validates the token</b><span>Signature, issuer, audience and expiry are checked against cached JWKS. Non-OIDC tokens can pass through via TokenReview.</span></div></li>
          <li><div><b>Claims become a Kubernetes identity</b><span>Username, groups and extras are mapped by claim or by CEL expression, with a prefix per issuer.</span></div></li>
          <li><div><b>The API server decides</b><span>The request is forwarded with the proxy's own ServiceAccount plus Impersonate headers. RBAC runs for the mapped user, and the audit log records them.</span></div></li>
        </ol>
        <div class="kop-callout"><b>What it changes:</b> the proxy's ServiceAccount may impersonate any user, so its Deployment and RBAC are privileged. Treat it like the API server itself.</div>
      </div>
      <CodeBlock id="kop-yaml" label="authentication-config.yaml" copy>
<Fragment set:html={`<span class="k">apiVersion</span>: apiserver.config.k8s.io/v1
<span class="k">kind</span>: AuthenticationConfiguration
<span class="k">jwt</span>:
  - <span class="k">issuer</span>:
      <span class="k">url</span>: <span class="s">https://accounts.google.com</span>
      <span class="k">audiences</span>: [my-google-client]
    <span class="k">claimMappings</span>:
      <span class="k">username</span>: { claim: email, prefix: <span class="s">"google:"</span> }
  - <span class="k">issuer</span>:
      <span class="k">url</span>: <span class="s">https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com</span>
      <span class="k">audiences</span>: [kube-oidc-proxy.example.com]
    <span class="k">claimMappings</span>:
      <span class="k">username</span>:
        <span class="k">expression</span>: <span class="s">'"gha:" + claims.repository + ":" + claims.ref'</span>
      <span class="k">groups</span>:
        <span class="k">expression</span>: <span class="s">'["gha:org:" + claims.repository_owner]'</span>`} />
      </CodeBlock>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
